---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';

const matrix = [
  { from: 'PS3 (DIST .psf, .big.edat)', recomp: ['ok', 'Yes'], skate: ['ok', 'Yes, via recomp'], ps3: ['', 'Already'] },
  { from: 'Xbox 360 / recomp (.xsf, .big)', recomp: ['', 'Already'], skate: ['ok', 'Yes'], ps3: ['warn', 'Planned'] },
  { from: '.skate (Rust engine)', recomp: ['warn', 'Planned'], skate: ['', 'Already'], ps3: ['warn', 'Planned'] },
];
---
<Base title="Map conversion" description="How skatemods converts Skate 3 maps between PS3, the native recomp and the Rust engine's .skate format, for free on GitHub Actions.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Map conversion" title="One upload, every platform" lede="Upload a Skate 3 map from any platform and get the others. The pipeline is open source, needs no game files, and runs on free GitHub Actions runners." />
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What converts today</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>From ↓ / To →</th><th>Recomp <code>.big</code></th><th><code>.skate</code></th><th>PS3</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {matrix.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{r.from}</th>
              {[r.recomp, r.skate, r.ps3].map(([tone, text]) => <td><span class={`chip ${tone}`}>{text}</span></td>)}
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Unpack.</strong> Archives (<code>.zip</code>, <code>.7z</code>, <code>.rar</code>) and EA big files (including PS3 <code>.big.edat</code>) are unpacked with path-traversal and size checks. Every <code>DIST_*</code> world inside is detected as PS3 (<code>.psf</code>) or Xbox 360 (<code>.xsf</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>PS3 → recomp.</strong> <a href="https://github.com/andrewnakas/skate3-ps3-to-x360">skate3-ps3-to-x360</a> rebuilds vertex and index buffers, vertex descriptors, mesh islands and textures in Xbox 360 form, then packages a standalone DLC <code>.big</code> with DlcBuilder.</li>
        <li><strong>Xbox 360 → .skate.</strong> The <a href="https://github.com/SK8-ENGINE/skate-3-rust-engine">Rust engine's</a> asset pipeline decodes the world, builds the retail collision archive and writes a <code>.skate</code> file.</li>
        <li><strong>Deliver.</strong> Each output is listed with its size, timing and a log. Anything the converter can't handle is refused and explained, never silently emitted wrong.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Proven on free runners</h2>
      <p>The first end-to-end run on GitHub's free <code>ubuntu-latest</code> runner, with no game data present:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Map</th><th>Path</th><th>Output</th><th>Time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>JumpCity</td><td>Xbox 360 → <code>.skate</code></td><td>95 MB</td><td>7 s</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sunbad Art Gallery</td><td>PS3 → recomp <code>.big</code></td><td>94 MB</td><td>4 s</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sunbad Art Gallery</td><td>PS3 → <code>.skate</code></td><td>47 MB</td><td>4 s</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Peak memory was under 0.5 GB per map. Run it yourself with the <a href="/guides/convert-ps3-maps/">CLI guide</a>.</p>

      <h2>What's next</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Accounts (sign in with GitHub) and uploads to storage with no download fees.</li>
        <li>A conversion job per upload, with live status and per-platform download buttons.</li>
        <li>An automatic check that rejects packs carrying stock EA assets, plus a takedown process. See the <a href="/about/">policy</a>.</li>
        <li>Reverse paths: recomp → PS3 and <code>.skate</code> → recomp.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
